# GPT-5.3 Codex Spark — findings by Iceman

- Source: OpenAI/GPT-5.3-Codex-Spark
- Date: 2026-11-10 (UTC)
- Overview and scoring methodology: `../../model-comparison.md`
- Cross-model signed log: `../../model-findings.md`

## Model card

- **Name:** GPT-5.3-Codex-Spark
- **Short description:** OpenAI’s GPT-5.3-Codex-Spark is a research-preview, Cerebras-served low-latency coding model (>1000 tok/s, 128K text-only) for real-time edits; retired 2026-09-14 per local metadata.
- **Provider / access:** OpenAI Codex (ChatGPT Pro preview / limited API partners). Local metadata lists `opencode/gpt-5.3-codex-spark`, no public per-token rate, and `noFreeId`.
- **Release / knowledge:** Official OpenAI announcement reviewed 2026-11-10. Knowledge cutoff not explicitly stated in reviewed source.
- **IDs:** `gpt-5.3-codex-spark`.
- **Context window:** 128,000 tokens total; 32,000 max output (metadata).
- **Modalities:** Text input/output (text-only preview).
- **Pricing (as of 2026-11-10):** No public first-party per-token rate (ChatGPT Pro preview/design-partner API); Zen third-party route $1.75/$14.00 per metadata.
- **Architecture:** Proprietary closed model, smaller Codex checkpoint served on Cerebras WSE-3 (announcement). Parameter count not publicly disclosed.

### Raw benchmarks found

> SELF-EXCLUSION: I reviewed OpenAI’s official GPT-5.3-Codex-Spark announcement, which states it demonstrates strong performance on SWE-Bench Pro and Terminal-Bench 2.0 and provides comparative charts/context, but the accessible extracted content did not provide clearly extractable, standardized numeric scores for this exact model in a verifiable form. Local metadata cites figures (e.g. Terminal-Bench 2.0 58.4%, SWE-Bench Pro 51.5%) but these were not independently verified from an accessible official table/text extract in this pass. To avoid unverifiable or misattributed scoring, this file is saved as `.md.excluded` (notes only; scores ignored).

